//? Title: FCN32s,16s and8s dense prediction skips
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Assigning a class to every pixel needs spatially aligned outputs from coarse CNN features. This report checks frozen bilinear filters and released FCN crop geometry, then fits all three compact VGG skip variants with explicit Adam and compares their held-out masks.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.7_segmentation/fcn.cpp`.

> The method

FCN replaces classification layers with spatial convolutions. Bilinear deconvolution restores resolution; projected intermediate VGG features add progressively finer class scores. Full released geometry and compact teaching geometry are checked separately before fitting.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/fcn_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/fcn_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/fcn_concept.tikz > build/fcn_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/fcn_concept.svg build/fcn_concept.dvi > build/fcn_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
