> Actual procedural image/mask pairs

The tensor shape generator creates64 fitting/16 validation/16 test96-pixel
RGB images with independent seeds11/22/33. Circle,rectangle and triangle
brightness/noise/tint have the same distributions, so labels require spatial
context. Later objects occlude earlier masks. This tensor RNG adaptation has
different fixed-seed pixels from the original mt19937 generator; it preserves
the procedural conventions rather than byte-for-byte samples. Four actual
fitting image/mask pairs appear below. The mask palette is background dark,
circle red,rectangle green,triangle blue.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fcn_data.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto data = m::TensorSegmentationShapes(64, 96, 11);
  std::vector<n::Tensor> gallery;
  const auto colored = m::ColorSegmentationLabels(n::slice_axis(data.labels, 0, 0, 4));
  for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
    gallery.push_back(n::slice_axis(data.images, 0, i, i + 1));
    gallery.push_back(n::slice_axis(colored, 0, i, i + 1));
  }
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(n::concat(gallery, 0), "build/fcn_data.png", 2, 0., 1., 3, 1., 2);
  const auto weights = m::SegmentationClassWeights(data.labels, 4);
  std::print(
      "64 fitting RGB images96x96; classes0 background,1 circle,2 rectangle,3 triangle. "
      "Fit-only inverse-square-root pseudocount weights {:.6f}/{:.6f}/{:.6f}/{:.6f}. "
      "Noise,tint and brightness are class-independent; later objects occlude earlier masks. "
      "Tensor RNG changes fixed-seed pixels relative to the old mt19937 generator.\n",
      weights.at({0}), weights.at({1}), weights.at({2}), weights.at({3}));
}
```
